# =============================================================================
# Workflow Lab .gitignore
# Sections: Gradle, IDEs, OS, logs, secrets, local databases, local agent files
# =============================================================================

### Gradle ###
.gradle/
.gradletasknamecache
# Build output, including the OpenAPI generated sources (build/generated/openapi).
# The generated code is never committed.
build/
# Keep the wrapper jar: it is how everyone gets the right Gradle version.
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
# A package may legitimately be called "build"; never ignore source directories.
!**/src/main/**/build/
!**/src/test/**/build/

### IntelliJ IDEA ###
# Ignore everything inside .idea EXCEPT the shared run configurations, so that
# opening the project gives a ready-to-use "Play" button. IntelliJ rewrites the
# other files (gradle.xml, misc.xml, ...) on every sync and they contain
# machine-specific paths, so sharing them only creates noise.
.idea/*
!.idea/runConfigurations/
*.iml
*.iws
*.ipr
out/
# IMPORTANT: this project has packages named "out" (domain.model.port.out).
# These exceptions stop the "out/" rule above from hiding that source code.
!**/src/main/**/out/
!**/src/test/**/out/

### Eclipse and VS Code ###
.vscode/
.classpath
.project
.settings/
bin/
!**/src/main/**/bin/
!**/src/test/**/bin/

### Operating system ###
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~

### Logs and temporary files ###
*.log
logs/
*.tmp
*.swp
*.bak

### Secrets and local configuration ###
# Never commit credentials. Share a template instead (for example .env.example).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
application-local.yaml
application-local.yml
application-local.properties
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore

### Local databases ###
# The app uses in-memory H2; these only appear if someone switches to a file database.
*.mv.db
*.trace.db
*.lock.db
*.h2.db

### Local files of coding agents ###
# AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md are shared; personal overrides are not.
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md
